Restore FUN_1000_4cd0 (walk) + FUN_1000_4ce7 (insert) far-pointer segment bases -- SMC trampoline list.

06bc registers a callback in a self-modifying-code linked list living in an un-decompiled scratch
region (~seg 0x1000 off 0x19bb). 4cd0 walks the list from the head (DS:SI, DS=0x1000 from 106d's
`push cs;pop ds`), following each node's forward far-pointer at [node+1] via `lds si,[si+1]` until the
terminator marker word 0xdb8b (mov bx,bx); 4ce7 then appends the new node (ES:BX = 0x1000:param_1)
after the last real node by splicing the far pointers. Ghidra dropped every far-pointer segment base
(the loaded offset was dereferenced as a host pointer -> SIGSEGV) -- the "dropped far/segment base on
string ops" class. Reconstruct all list accesses as g_mem+(seg<<4)+off with the segment threaded
(0x1000 for this sole call path, the caller CS in the base-0 FUN_1000_* model); nodes are passed
between 4cd0 and 4ce7 as far pointers (seg<<16|off). The thunks are inert for our C-compiled control
flow (we never execute g_mem as code) but the list memory is kept byte-faithful to the original.

